{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1483559-is-there-a-way-to-gain-an-attainment-without-the-normal-prerequisite-arcana-dots","id":1483559,"title":"Is there a way to gain an attainment without the normal prerequisite arcana dots?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-09T23:35:15-07:00","id":1483559,"title":"Is there a way to gain an attainment without the normal prerequisite arcana dots?","content":"Basically the title says it all, I want access to an attainment (specifically the space 4 attainment that lets you mess with scope) but I don't want the character to actually have 4 dots of space, as I would rather they not be able to teleport around. Artifacts can have attainments but as I read it, only for their specific one effect. Is there some way I don't know of to apply an attainment you don't normally have to your own spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T23:58:44-07:00","id":1483561,"title":"","content":"To answer the question of the header: By RAW, no.<br /> As for your specific conundrum, a Merit seems to be the obvious answer. The question is the cost. By the book, Attainments are worth 1 Experience, but they are clearly undercosted (like many supernatural advantages of the Awakened) in that regard, given their utlity, compared to regular Merits. It is mostly up to you how much of an investment you want to make this. It sounds like you actively *want* them to use it, so it should be cheap. Perhaps you simply give them the ability for free.<br /> <br /> As a personal aside from me though, while definitely useful, I would be loathe to give characters the option to use less Reach too easily. Reach (and OverReaching) is important and anything that makes Paradox easier to manage is iffy in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T13:17:31-07:00","id":1483645,"title":"","content":"By RAW, there are certain Grimmoires that can teach Attainments, but I think the default ones for the Arcana are not covered by that. <br /> <br /> Normally, the easiest way to use higher spell scale would be to use AoE spells. But without some Fate magic, it will affect everything within the area. Having a Fate mage bless you so you can have extra dice for spell factors also works.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, just invest time. Taking the time to cast with ritual time gets you a +1 bonus for each additional interval taken, up to +5 and without counting as a yantra. Then mix with a ritual time cleaning yantra for +2, which combined High Speech and runes should allow you to have enough factors for just about anything.<br /> <br /> Lastly, in <i>Grimmoire of Grimmoires</i> there is the mention of the Hildebrand Recording, an Abyssal tape which sends Paradox somewhere. Probably not somewhere good and it definitely will come back to bite the user, but its an option. Provided, of course, that the cabal is able to evade the mafia don that wants it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T14:55:40-07:00","id":1483652,"title":"","content":"Let's take a step back here:<br /> <br /> Why don't you want the character to teleport around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T18:21:03-07:00","id":1483667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1483559-is-there-a-way-to-gain-an-attainment-without-the-normal-prerequisite-arcana-dots?p=1483645#post1483645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Normally, the easiest way to use higher spell scale would be to use AoE spells. But without some Fate magic, it will affect everything within the area. Having a Fate mage bless you so you can have extra dice for spell factors also works.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, just invest time. Taking the time to cast with ritual time gets you a +1 bonus for each additional interval taken, up to +5 and without counting as a yantra. Then mix with a ritual time cleaning yantra for +2, which combined High Speech and runes should allow you to have enough factors for just about anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>The four-dot Space Attainment doesn't actually help with covering the Scale factor, it just gives you the option to spend a point of Mana instead of Reaching to get the Advanced table.<br /> <br /> Which is useful, certainly, but to be honest I don't think it's such a big distinction that you'd be so pressed as to want some special alternative means of accessing it.<br /> <br /> It almost reads to me like the original post misunderstood it a bit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T01:51:41-07:00","id":1484184,"title":"","content":"I will admit I somehow forgot you could go beyond the &quot;Free Reach&quot; you get for dots. I have spent too long trying to be responsible and never even risk a paradox I flat out forgot you could reach past that limit, now that I have remembered that fact: you are correct that finding some weird workaround is more trouble than it is worth. As far as not wanting to teleport it is partly a character decision that I don't want to have access to that sort of easy movement, and partly to avoid potentially stepping on the toes of another mage player who has bunches of space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T19:16:11-07:00","id":1484324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1483559-is-there-a-way-to-gain-an-attainment-without-the-normal-prerequisite-arcana-dots?p=1484184#post1484184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will admit I somehow forgot you could go beyond the &quot;Free Reach&quot; you get for dots. I have spent too long trying to be responsible and never even risk a paradox I flat out forgot you could reach past that limit, now that I have remembered that fact: you are correct that finding some weird workaround is more trouble than it is worth. As far as not wanting to teleport it is partly a character decision that I don't want to have access to that sort of easy movement, and partly to avoid potentially stepping on the toes of another mage player who has bunches of space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it does come with challenges. First is that containing Paradox hurts, causing resistant bashing damage. You can also use mana to diminish it, but that can eat your stores quickly and take multiple turns to cast a spell you need now.<br /> <br /> There is an option of using two dedicated tools to diminish the impact, but that comes with the challenge of requiring you to incorporate them into spells far more often.<br /> <br /> Plus Paradox is a cascading problem. Once you over Reached in a scene, it will affect <b>every single</b> spellcasting roll for the scene, adding one more Paradox dice each time. Failing to contain the Paradox fully gives an Abyssal condition, which can make things much worse and prompt this problem to repeat over multiple scenes. You could scour the Paradox condition out, but that gives a point of resistant lethal damage (2 days to heal) and uses a Pattern Scouring for the day.<br /> <br /> Over Reaching is a calculated risk and sometimes the best option, but its very easy for the momentum to build beyond what you can deal with. Its easy when you are low Gnosis, since there are fewer Paradox dice per over Reach. But its mages who get comfortable with that situation who tend to fall prey to those the domino effect as they grow in power. Being cautious with it is pretty understandable.<br /> <br /> On the matter of overlap, every mage has a different way they think about, employ and understand an Arcanum. Just because you both have it does not mean you both will use them the same way. This is especially true if someone does not have it as a Ruling Arcanum, which means they will need to spend mana to use improvised spells with it. In addition, the different combination of Arcana each player has means it can be incorporated with them to create pretty distinct spells. It also gives the GM the freedom to throw more problems involving this Arcanum at the cabal, some of which could be tackled in parallel and tailored to your individual styles and approaches. Lastly, it also means you can use teamwork spellcasting far more effectively, which can lead to awesome moments highlighting the cabal's sheer power as you progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-18-2022, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T05:07:38-07:00","id":1484348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1483559-is-there-a-way-to-gain-an-attainment-without-the-normal-prerequisite-arcana-dots?p=1484324#post1484324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus Paradox is a cascading problem. Once you over Reached in a scene, it will affect <b>every single</b> spellcasting roll for the scene, adding one more Paradox dice each time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two corrections:<br /> <br /> You gain a cumulative Paradox roll bonus every time you risk Paradox, not just from overreaching.<br /> <br /> Unlike other sources of Paradox dice, the cumulative bonus is conditional. That means it only applies when you already risk Paradox. If you cast a spell that would not risk Paradox, the bonus isn't applied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T07:50:31-07:00","id":1484354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1483559-is-there-a-way-to-gain-an-attainment-without-the-normal-prerequisite-arcana-dots?p=1484348#post1484348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two corrections:<br /> <br /> You gain a cumulative Paradox roll bonus every time you risk Paradox, not just from overreaching.<br /> <br /> Unlike other sources of Paradox dice, the cumulative bonus is conditional. That means it only applies when you already risk Paradox. If you cast a spell that would not risk Paradox, the bonus isn't applied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, for the longest time I thought even risking a Paradox roll added to the total and from then on you had the Abyss' attention on your Imagos. So long as you don't over Reach too much, its as insane. One more clarification please, does a Paradox that didn't succeed (one reduced to a chance die that failed) still become a +1 on the next Paradox roll ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T08:01:15-07:00","id":1484357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1483559-is-there-a-way-to-gain-an-attainment-without-the-normal-prerequisite-arcana-dots?p=1484354#post1484354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, for the longest time I thought even risking a Paradox roll added to the total and from then on you had the Abyss' attention on your Imagos. So long as you don't over Reach too much, its as insane. One more clarification please, does a Paradox that didn't succeed (one reduced to a chance die that failed) still become a +1 on the next Paradox roll ?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<b>Each Paradox roll</b> after the first made for the same caster within the same scene. This bonus accumulates with <b>each roll</b>, so the third roll made for a mage within a scene has a +2 modifier.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}